there's zero response from the youth leadership,

252
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:15,520
we're going to need to respond

253
00:13:15,520 --> 00:13:17,280
because, as you've stated,

254
00:13:17,920 --> 00:13:20,640
there's more than just their interests

255
00:13:20,640 --> 00:13:22,080
and their development in question.

256
00:13:22,080 --> 00:13:24,000
There's another of other scouts

257
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:25,600
and families involved in this too.

258
00:13:26,320 --> 00:13:27,760
Now, there have been plenty of times

259
00:13:27,760 --> 00:13:28,800
in the past 30 years

260
00:13:28,800 --> 00:13:30,160
my patrol leaders council

261
00:13:30,160 --> 00:13:32,400
has just totally dropped the ball.

262
00:13:32,400 --> 00:13:34,880
They've done absolutely nothing.

263
00:13:34,880 --> 00:13:36,000
Now, when this happens,

264
00:13:36,640 --> 00:13:37,520
I don't just say,

265
00:13:37,520 --> 00:13:39,680
well, this is a boy led thing

266
00:13:39,680 --> 00:13:41,920
and we can't really do too much about it.

267
00:13:41,920 --> 00:13:44,480
No, I have a frank heart to heart

268
00:13:44,480 --> 00:13:45,600
with the senior patrol leader

269
00:13:45,600 --> 00:13:48,400
and I tell him in no uncertain terms:

270
00:13:48,400 --> 00:13:49,520
you need to get moving.

271
00:13:50,240 --> 00:13:52,960
And normally he will take a step

272
00:13:52,960 --> 00:13:53,760
in my direction.

273
00:13:54,320 --> 00:13:56,000
It might not be a whole lot,

274
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:57,520
but he moves a little bit

275
00:13:57,520 --> 00:13:58,880
and I respond with all kinds

276
00:13:58,880 --> 00:14:00,800
of supporting and encouragement.

277
00:14:00,800 --> 00:14:04,000
Sometimes this is like pulling teeth

278
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:07,040
and sometimes it involves

279
00:14:07,040 --> 00:14:08,320
a lot of hand holding

280
00:14:08,320 --> 00:14:10,160
and sometimes feeding them information

281
00:14:10,160 --> 00:14:11,040
to work with.

282
00:14:11,120 --> 00:14:12,719
but I need to get them

283
00:14:12,719 --> 00:14:14,719
in the process of doing it.

284
00:14:14,719 --> 00:14:16,800
I'm looking for the least indication

285
00:14:16,800 --> 00:14:18,400
of initiative in building on it.

286
00:14:18,400 --> 00:14:20,160
You can't just necessarily,

287
00:14:20,160 --> 00:14:22,160
in every situation like this,

288
00:14:22,160 --> 00:14:23,599
draw a hard line and say,

289
00:14:23,599 --> 00:14:25,920
well, unless they do a,

290
00:14:25,920 --> 00:14:27,520
we're not going to do B.

291
00:14:27,520 --> 00:14:30,880
No, sometimes you have to make a happen

292
00:14:30,880 --> 00:14:33,199
and then build on the initiative

293
00:14:33,199 --> 00:14:35,280
that they respond with.

294
00:14:35,280 --> 00:14:37,360
Simply letting things like this slide

295
00:14:37,360 --> 00:14:38,719
for weeks at a time

296
00:14:38,719 --> 00:14:40,079
is not right

297
00:14:40,080 --> 00:14:42,720
And it approaches the logical absurdity

298
00:14:42,720 --> 00:14:43,920
that I mentioned earlier.

299
00:14:43,920 --> 00:14:45,920
If this was a football team

300
00:14:45,920 --> 00:14:47,040
and the team showed up

301
00:14:47,040 --> 00:14:49,360
and they just laid down on the sidelines

302
00:14:49,360 --> 00:14:50,400
with the coaches just say:

303
00:14:50,400 --> 00:14:51,840
well, you know, it's their decision,

304
00:14:51,840 --> 00:14:53,120
There's nothing we can do about it?

305
00:14:53,760 --> 00:14:54,720
No, I hope not.

306
00:14:54,720 --> 00:14:56,080
I hope they'd make some demands

307
00:14:56,080 --> 00:14:57,280
and issue some directions,

308
00:14:57,280 --> 00:15:00,640
And sometimes that's what needs to happen,

309
00:15:00,640 --> 00:15:02,320
Not as a matter of habit,

310
00:15:02,320 --> 00:15:03,440
where the adults are making

311
00:15:03,440 --> 00:15:04,240
all the decision,

312
00:15:04,240 --> 00:15:05,920
issuing all the directions

313
00:15:05,920 --> 00:15:08,880
and constantly micromanaging

314
00:15:08,880 --> 00:15:10,720
everything that the scouts do,

315
00:15:10,720 --> 00:15:13,120
But sometimes, if youth leaders

316
00:15:13,120 --> 00:15:14,240
are unresponsive,

317
00:15:14,880 --> 00:15:16,400
they need to be encouraged

318
00:15:16,400 --> 00:15:17,439
in every way possible

319
00:15:17,439 --> 00:15:18,720
to make a response,

320
00:15:18,720 --> 00:15:20,640
And then you build on that.

321
00:15:21,520 --> 00:15:22,320
While it's true

322
00:15:22,320 --> 00:15:23,920
we should foster and encourage

323
00:15:23,920 --> 00:15:24,800
youth engagement,

324
00:15:24,800 --> 00:15:27,760
It's never an on and off switch.

325
00:15:27,760 --> 00:15:29,200
There's a lot of different levels

326
00:15:29,200 --> 00:15:30,960
of ability and leadership

327
00:15:30,960 --> 00:15:32,320
and experience

328
00:15:32,320 --> 00:15:34,000
and the appropriate responses

329
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:34,720
to those levels.

330
00:15:34,720 --> 00:15:35,760
that's demanded of us.

331
00:15:36,320 --> 00:15:38,000
Now, I don't understand

332
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:40,240
how anybody who's part of a committee

333
00:15:40,240 --> 00:15:41,760
and has been tasked

334
00:15:41,760 --> 00:15:44,880
with things that require information

335
00:15:44,880 --> 00:15:46,080
beforehand

336
00:15:46,080 --> 00:15:47,600
can overstep their bounds

337
00:15:47,600 --> 00:15:49,520
by asking for that information.

338
00:15:49,520 --> 00:15:50,880
I mean, it doesn't seem

339
00:15:50,880 --> 00:15:52,000
very logical to me.

340
00:15:52,560 --> 00:15:54,480
How exactly is a perfectly

341
00:15:54,480 --> 00:15:56,080
reasonable request like that?

342
00:15:56,800 --> 00:15:57,920
Somehow you're surping

343
00:15:57,920 --> 00:15:58,800
the scouts ability

344
00:15:58,800 --> 00:15:59,680
to make decisions.

345
00:15:59,680 --> 00:16:00,720
I don't see it.

346
00:16:00,720 --> 00:16:01,840
I hope this begins

347
00:16:01,840 --> 00:16:02,960
to shed a little bit of light

348
00:16:02,960 --> 00:16:03,440
on the matter.

349
00:16:04,080 --> 00:16:04,560
In short,

350
00:16:04,560 --> 00:16:05,600
it appears to me that

351
00:16:05,600 --> 00:16:07,120
the attentions of the adults

352
00:16:07,120 --> 00:16:08,240
involved are good.

353
00:16:08,240 --> 00:16:09,920
They're just getting the execution

354
00:16:09,920 --> 00:16:11,200
flawed a little bit.

355
00:16:11,200 --> 00:16:13,040
Not knowing any of the personalities

356
00:16:13,040 --> 00:16:14,400
or mitigating circumstances

357
00:16:14,400 --> 00:16:14,800
involved,

358
00:16:14,800 --> 00:16:16,080
I don't want to cast my advice

359
00:16:16,080 --> 00:16:18,000
of judgment about who's right

360
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:19,120
or wrong,

361
00:16:19,120 --> 00:16:20,800
but these are observations

362
00:16:20,800 --> 00:16:21,920
based on what you've told me

363
00:16:21,920 --> 00:16:22,960
and my own experience,

364
00:16:22,960 --> 00:16:23,760
because you know

365
00:16:23,760 --> 00:16:25,120
I've been as guilty of this

366
00:16:25,120 --> 00:16:25,920
as anyone else.

367
00:16:26,560 --> 00:16:27,680
I want to take notice

368
00:16:27,680 --> 00:16:28,320
of your statement

369
00:16:28,320 --> 00:16:29,680
about domineering men

370
00:16:29,680 --> 00:16:31,520
and, in as much as it's possible,

371
00:16:31,520 --> 00:16:33,360
let me apologize for them.

372
00:16:33,360 --> 00:16:34,400
I know it's not

373
00:16:34,400 --> 00:16:35,280
really possible,

374
00:16:35,280 --> 00:16:36,800
but perhaps it helps a little

375
00:16:37,360 --> 00:16:37,920
to let you know

376
00:16:37,920 --> 00:16:39,360
that I do understand

377
00:16:39,360 --> 00:16:40,800
what you're talking about.

378
00:16:40,800 --> 00:16:42,080
I've observed men and boys

379
00:16:42,080 --> 00:16:42,720
working together

380
00:16:42,720 --> 00:16:45,040
and scouting for a long time now

381
00:16:45,040 --> 00:16:46,080
and there are many different

382
00:16:46,080 --> 00:16:47,120
attitudes and actions

383
00:16:47,120 --> 00:16:48,560
to be overcome. sometimes

384
00:16:49,440 --> 00:16:51,040
Many of us men mistake

385
00:16:51,040 --> 00:16:52,720
being compassionate or helpful

386
00:16:52,720 --> 00:16:54,320
for being unmanly.

387
00:16:54,320 --> 00:16:55,360
Many of us think we need

388
00:16:55,360 --> 00:16:56,400
to make a scout's way

389
00:16:56,400 --> 00:16:57,360
difficult because

390
00:16:57,360 --> 00:16:58,400
this will somehow

391
00:16:58,400 --> 00:16:59,600
help them become tough

392
00:16:59,600 --> 00:17:00,320
and be a man.

393
00:17:01,120 --> 00:17:02,720
But to be brutally honest,

394
00:17:02,720 --> 00:17:03,680
we sometimes get

395
00:17:03,680 --> 00:17:04,880
disappointed and angry

396
00:17:04,880 --> 00:17:05,600
with our sons

397
00:17:05,600 --> 00:17:06,480
and with our scouts

398
00:17:06,879 --> 00:17:08,480
because we see a lot of ourselves

399
00:17:08,480 --> 00:17:09,200
in them.

400
00:17:09,200 --> 00:17:11,200
It's a painful thing for us

401
00:17:11,200 --> 00:17:12,639
and sometimes we react

402
00:17:12,639 --> 00:17:13,599
by striking back

403
00:17:13,599 --> 00:17:15,440
with meanness and harshness

404
00:17:15,440 --> 00:17:16,560
instead of responding

405
00:17:16,560 --> 00:17:17,680
with some compassion

406
00:17:17,680 --> 00:17:19,040
and understanding.

407
00:17:19,040 --> 00:17:20,639
I think men a lot of times

408
00:17:20,639 --> 00:17:22,079
distrust compassion

409
00:17:22,079 --> 00:17:23,680
because we fear

410
00:17:23,680 --> 00:17:26,560
it will make our boys soft,

411
00:17:26,560 --> 00:17:28,319
It will make them somewhat

412
00:17:28,319 --> 00:17:30,000
less than real men.

413
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:31,760
We fear the apron strings

414
00:17:31,760 --> 00:17:32,399
of childhood

415
00:17:32,399 --> 00:17:33,440
and we feel it's important

416
00:17:33,440 --> 00:17:34,399
to break them,

417
00:17:34,399 --> 00:17:35,840
and the way we do that

418
00:17:35,840 --> 00:17:38,080
isn't very pretty sometimes,

419
00:17:38,080 --> 00:17:39,520
Frankly. there are a lot of us

420
00:17:39,520 --> 00:17:41,520
who imitate our own upbringing

421
00:17:41,520 --> 00:17:42,959
and in our parenting-

422
00:17:42,959 --> 00:17:44,399
for good or ill,

423
00:17:44,399 --> 00:17:46,240
because it's all we really know.

424
00:17:46,240 --> 00:17:47,199
There's always been a

425
00:17:47,199 --> 00:17:48,879
tension between men and women,

426
00:17:48,879 --> 00:17:49,919
mothers and fathers

427
00:17:49,919 --> 00:17:51,520
about this type of thing,

428
00:17:51,520 --> 00:17:52,800
and that tension is just

429
00:17:52,800 --> 00:17:53,760
as real and scouting

430
00:17:53,760 --> 00:17:54,639
as anywhere else.

431
00:17:54,639 --> 00:17:56,320
What we all ought to do,

432
00:17:56,320 --> 00:17:57,840
men and women alike,

433
00:17:57,840 --> 00:17:58,959
is to take stock

434
00:17:58,959 --> 00:18:00,159
of our own reactions

435
00:18:00,159 --> 00:18:00,959
and feelings

436
00:18:00,959 --> 00:18:02,000
and do our best

437
00:18:02,560 --> 00:18:04,480
to rise to the higher ideals

438
00:18:04,560 --> 00:18:06,320
and potential in the scout oath and law.

439
00:18:06,320 --> 00:18:07,680
What you come to realize

440
00:18:07,680 --> 00:18:08,960
as a scouter

441
00:18:08,960 --> 00:18:10,720
is that you are growing

442
00:18:10,720 --> 00:18:11,680
and developing

443
00:18:11,680 --> 00:18:12,880
and learning

444
00:18:12,880 --> 00:18:14,720
right along with the scouts.

445
00:18:14,720 --> 00:18:15,840
It's pretty amazing

446
00:18:15,840 --> 00:18:17,200
and it's a pretty great thing

447
00:18:17,200 --> 00:18:19,360
about being involved in scouting.

448
00:18:19,360 --> 00:18:21,280
The second email I received

449
00:18:21,280 --> 00:18:22,320
was from a gentleman

450
00:18:22,320 --> 00:18:23,360
who said this:

451
00:18:23,360 --> 00:18:24,720
I've just accepted the request

452
00:18:24,720 --> 00:18:26,240
to become a scout master

453
00:18:26,240 --> 00:18:27,440
and I hope to guide our troop

454
00:18:27,440 --> 00:18:29,600
away from adult leadership

455
00:18:29,600 --> 00:18:30,560
towards the scouts

456
00:18:30,560 --> 00:18:31,760
leading themselves.

457
00:18:31,760 --> 00:18:33,360
I have purchased the book

458
00:18:33,360 --> 00:18:34,960
Working the Patrol Method

459
00:18:34,960 --> 00:18:36,560
and I will read it as soon as I get it.

460
00:18:36,560 --> 00:18:37,280
Can you let me know

461
00:18:37,280 --> 00:18:38,640
if there are any other resources

462
00:18:38,640 --> 00:18:39,360
that may help.

463
00:18:39,920 --> 00:18:41,200
I want to also know

464
00:18:41,200 --> 00:18:42,800
what training is best

465
00:18:42,800 --> 00:18:43,920
to do first

466
00:18:43,920 --> 00:18:45,520
as a new scout master,

467
00:18:45,520 --> 00:18:46,960
and what's the best course

468
00:18:46,960 --> 00:18:48,560
for training youth leaders.

469
00:18:48,560 --> 00:18:49,680
Well, first of all,

470
00:18:49,680 --> 00:18:51,920
congratulations on becoming a scout master.

471
00:18:51,920 --> 00:18:53,200
It's great fun,

472
00:18:53,200 --> 00:18:54,720
It's a big challenge.

473
00:18:54,720 --> 00:18:55,760
Now, whatever has happened

474
00:18:55,760 --> 00:18:56,320
in the past

475
00:18:56,320 --> 00:18:57,600
and whatever your ambitions

476
00:18:57,600 --> 00:18:58,560
for the future

477
00:18:58,560 --> 00:18:59,440
of the troop,

478
00:18:59,440 --> 00:19:00,880
your first responsibility

479
00:19:00,880 --> 00:19:01,920
is always delivering

480
00:19:01,920 --> 00:19:03,200
the program to the scouts,

481
00:19:03,200 --> 00:19:04,800
And I think you get that.

482
00:19:04,800 --> 00:19:05,920
I'll hazard the guess

483
00:19:05,920 --> 00:19:07,920
that, based on what I hear and see,

484
00:19:08,800 --> 00:19:10,000
the majority of scouts

485
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:11,120
are members and troops

486
00:19:11,120 --> 00:19:12,080
just like yours,

487
00:19:12,080 --> 00:19:13,840
that kind of are more adult

488
00:19:13,840 --> 00:19:14,640
than youth, led,

489
00:19:15,280 --> 00:19:16,640
maybe not really applying

490
00:19:16,640 --> 00:19:17,520
the patrol system

491
00:19:17,520 --> 00:19:19,200
and just kind of chugging along

492
00:19:19,200 --> 00:19:20,240
like they always have.

493
00:19:21,360 --> 00:19:22,880
I'd agree that this isn't

494
00:19:22,880 --> 00:19:25,440
necessarily the optimal experience,

495
00:19:25,440 --> 00:19:26,080
but remember,

496
00:19:26,080 --> 00:19:27,520
it's not doing any harm.

497
00:19:27,520 --> 00:19:28,240
as a matter of fact,

498
00:19:28,240 --> 00:19:29,440
it's doing a lot of good.

499
00:19:30,080 --> 00:19:31,360
My point is

500
00:19:32,160 --> 00:19:33,600
this isn't an emergency.

501
00:19:34,160 --> 00:19:35,840
Things are not going to change

502
00:19:35,840 --> 00:19:37,840
into what you'd like to see quickly.

503
00:19:38,400 --> 00:19:40,160
It's going to take a little time

504
00:19:40,160 --> 00:19:41,440
and it will require a lot of

505
00:19:41,440 --> 00:19:42,880
forbearance and patience

506
00:19:42,880 --> 00:19:43,520
on your part.

507
00:19:43,520 --> 00:19:44,960
Now it's going to be great fun

508
00:19:45,520 --> 00:19:47,280
and things are going to change,

509
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:49,680
but I'm just going to encourage

510
00:19:49,680 --> 00:19:50,640
you: don't rush,

511
00:19:50,640 --> 00:19:51,360
don't push

512
00:19:51,360 --> 00:19:52,640
and don't fret too much.

513
00:19:53,280 --> 00:19:54,400
Stay on the course.

514
00:19:54,960 --> 00:19:56,480
make these changes,

515
00:19:56,480 --> 00:19:58,160
work with your scouts

516
00:19:58,160 --> 00:19:59,680
and you're going to get there.

517
00:19:59,680 --> 00:20:00,800
You've got a good start

518
00:20:00,800 --> 00:20:02,080
with the patrol method book.

519
00:20:02,080 --> 00:20:03,840
it's a great resource

520
00:20:03,840 --> 00:20:05,360
and I'm going to send you a copy

521
00:20:05,360 --> 00:20:06,000
of my book,

522
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:07,040
The Scouting Journey,

523
00:20:07,040 --> 00:20:08,000
see if that helps.

524
00:20:08,720 --> 00:20:10,240
As for which training to take first,

525
00:20:10,240 --> 00:20:11,280
you know it's fairly kind of

526
00:20:11,280 --> 00:20:12,000
dry

527
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:13,200
what a scout master needs

528
00:20:13,200 --> 00:20:14,720
to be considered trained.

529
00:20:14,720 --> 00:20:17,200
so I would do that course of training

530
00:20:17,200 --> 00:20:19,280
and then take whatever time allows.

531
00:20:19,919 --> 00:20:20,560
do it all.

532
00:20:20,560 --> 00:20:21,919
take all the online training

533
00:20:21,919 --> 00:20:22,480
that you can,

534
00:20:22,480 --> 00:20:23,919
take all the in-person training

535
00:20:23,919 --> 00:20:24,480
that you can.

536
00:20:25,360 --> 00:20:27,440
It certainly won't hurt, right?

537
00:20:27,440 --> 00:20:28,800
As for what training course

538
00:20:28,800 --> 00:20:30,159
I recommend for youth leaders,

539
00:20:30,160 --> 00:20:31,360
I really don't.

540
00:20:31,360 --> 00:20:32,720
I don't think that youth leaders

541
00:20:32,720 --> 00:20:33,840
respond very well

542
00:20:33,840 --> 00:20:35,520
to that kind of event-based

543
00:20:35,520 --> 00:20:37,600
or course-based training.

544
00:20:37,600 --> 00:20:39,120
A lot of skills they need

545
00:20:39,120 --> 00:20:41,200
actually come pretty easy to them

546
00:20:41,200 --> 00:20:43,520
if you give them some space to develop.

547
00:20:43,520 --> 00:20:45,760
Now let me get on my soapbox

548
00:20:45,760 --> 00:20:47,120
here for a second.

549
00:20:47,120 --> 00:20:48,240
How do you show somebody

550
00:20:48,240 --> 00:20:49,840
how to tie a square knot?

551
00:20:49,840 --> 00:20:50,800
You don't sit them down

552
00:20:50,800 --> 00:20:52,320
to a PowerPoint presentation

553
00:20:52,320 --> 00:20:53,200
on the history of

554
00:20:53,200 --> 00:20:54,000
cordage

555
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:55,280
and knotting theory, right.

556
00:20:55,840 --> 00:20:56,480
You get a rope

557
00:20:56,480 --> 00:20:57,600
and you show them.

558
00:20:57,600 --> 00:20:58,480
How do you

559
00:20:58,480 --> 00:20:59,200
share a game

560
00:20:59,200 --> 00:21:00,240
or a song with scouts?

561
00:21:00,240 --> 00:21:01,200
Do you sit them down?

562
00:21:01,200 --> 00:21:01,760
sit them down

563
00:21:01,760 --> 00:21:02,960
and draw a diagram of the game

564
00:21:02,960 --> 00:21:04,160
and go through all the rules

565
00:21:04,160 --> 00:21:06,080
and permutations of the game,

566
00:21:06,080 --> 00:21:07,120
or do you start playing

567
00:21:07,120 --> 00:21:08,560
and learn as you go along?

568
00:21:08,560 --> 00:21:09,200
If you're going to teach

569
00:21:09,200 --> 00:21:10,240
scouts to sing a song,

570
00:21:10,240 --> 00:21:11,600
do you hand out song sheets

571
00:21:11,600 --> 00:21:13,360
and rehearse the harmonies

572
00:21:13,360 --> 00:21:14,240
before you start,

573
00:21:14,240 --> 00:21:15,760
or do you just start singing?

574
00:21:15,760 --> 00:21:17,360
I just start singing. personally,

575
00:21:17,920 --> 00:21:19,040
Scouts don't want

576
00:21:19,040 --> 00:21:20,720
or care much about theory.

577
00:21:21,600 --> 00:21:22,800
They want action.

578
00:21:22,800 --> 00:21:23,920
Now, this is not to say

579
00:21:23,920 --> 00:21:24,480
that it's a

580
00:21:24,480 --> 00:21:26,240
that a little instruction is bad.

581
00:21:26,800 --> 00:21:28,400
I don't say that's bad,

582
00:21:28,400 --> 00:21:30,240
but what needs to come first

583
00:21:30,240 --> 00:21:31,360
is action.

584
00:21:31,360 --> 00:21:32,640
You won't fix things

585
00:21:32,640 --> 00:21:34,000
by sitting all the youth leaders

586
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:34,880
down on a weekend

587
00:21:34,880 --> 00:21:36,000
and describing how things

588
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:36,720
are going to change,

589
00:21:37,280 --> 00:21:38,320
because we aren't talking

590
00:21:38,320 --> 00:21:39,920
about throwing a switch here.

591
00:21:39,920 --> 00:21:40,640
Right,

592
00:21:40,640 --> 00:21:42,480
It isn't that easy.

593
00:21:42,480 --> 00:21:43,360
What happens

594
00:21:43,360 --> 00:21:44,240
if you show up

595
00:21:44,240 --> 00:21:45,360
at the next scout meeting

596
00:21:45,360 --> 00:21:46,320
and you ask the senior

597
00:21:46,320 --> 00:21:47,680
patrol leader what his job is?

598
00:21:48,240 --> 00:21:49,600
Ask him to tell you

599
00:21:49,600 --> 00:21:50,960
What does he think his job is,

600
00:21:51,600 --> 00:21:52,400
What does he think

601
00:21:52,400 --> 00:21:53,360
he should be doing

602
00:21:53,360 --> 00:21:54,640
that he's not doing

603
00:21:54,640 --> 00:21:55,520
And what would he like

604
00:21:55,520 --> 00:21:56,400
to stop doing?

605
00:21:57,200 --> 00:21:58,560
I mean, maybe it's just

606
00:21:58,560 --> 00:21:59,600
making announcements

607
00:21:59,600 --> 00:22:00,800
at the closing of the meeting,

608
00:22:00,800 --> 00:22:02,160
or something simple

609
00:22:02,160 --> 00:22:03,920
that the adults are used to doing

610
00:22:03,920 --> 00:22:05,680
that the scout should take over,

611
00:22:05,680 --> 00:22:06,960
If you handle this right

612
00:22:07,600 --> 00:22:08,400
in your discussion

613
00:22:08,400 --> 00:22:09,520
with the senior patrol leader.

614
00:22:09,520 --> 00:22:10,320
he's going to go home

615
00:22:10,320 --> 00:22:12,240
thinking it was his idea all along.

616
00:22:12,880 --> 00:22:13,760
Of course you'll have to

617
00:22:13,760 --> 00:22:14,560
corral the adults

618
00:22:14,560 --> 00:22:15,440
and get them to stop

619
00:22:15,440 --> 00:22:16,400
doing some things,

620
00:22:16,400 --> 00:22:18,000
and that can be a bigger challenge.

621
00:22:18,560 --> 00:22:20,080
But they chose you

622
00:22:20,080 --> 00:22:21,440
to become the scout master

623
00:22:21,440 --> 00:22:22,320
and they're going to follow

624
00:22:22,320 --> 00:22:23,520
your directions.

625
00:22:23,520 --> 00:22:24,560
Maybe not at first,

626
00:22:25,120 --> 00:22:26,320
maybe not joyfully,

627
00:22:26,560 --> 00:22:27,760
but ultimately

628
00:22:27,760 --> 00:22:29,439
they're going to get on board.

629
00:22:29,439 --> 00:22:30,480
Don't drop hints

630
00:22:30,480 --> 00:22:31,760
or ask questions of adults.

631
00:22:31,760 --> 00:22:32,960
You give them directions.

632
00:22:32,960 --> 00:22:34,720
Here's a key thing to remember

633
00:22:34,720 --> 00:22:36,720
and I've often repeated it here:

634
00:22:36,720 --> 00:22:38,159
The scout master mentors

635
00:22:38,159 --> 00:22:39,679
and coaches as youth leaders,

636
00:22:39,679 --> 00:22:40,879
but he directs

637
00:22:40,879 --> 00:22:42,639
and leads adults.

638
00:22:42,639 --> 00:22:43,600
Of course you'll be

639
00:22:43,600 --> 00:22:44,960
good natured and affable,

640
00:22:44,960 --> 00:22:45,919
but firm.

641
00:22:45,919 --> 00:22:47,200
when you're talking with adults,

642
00:22:47,760 --> 00:22:49,600
You're jumping into the volcano.

643
00:22:49,600 --> 00:22:50,399
It's hot in here

644
00:22:50,399 --> 00:22:51,360
and it's challenging,

645
00:22:51,360 --> 00:22:52,000
hard work,

646
00:22:52,000 --> 00:22:53,360
but it's great fun.

647
00:22:53,360 --> 00:22:55,120
It's really great fun.

648
00:22:55,120 --> 00:22:56,320
I hope all this makes sense.

649
00:22:56,320 --> 00:22:57,120
I wish I could give you

650
00:22:57,120 --> 00:22:58,880
three easy steps to success,

651
00:22:58,880 --> 00:22:59,920
but I can't.

652
00:22:59,920 --> 00:23:01,680
95% of your work

653
00:23:01,680 --> 00:23:02,480
as a scouter

654
00:23:02,480 --> 00:23:03,840
is attitude

655
00:23:03,840 --> 00:23:04,720
and spirit.

656
00:23:04,720 --> 00:23:05,680
The skills and knowledge

657
00:23:05,680 --> 00:23:06,960
come with experience,

658
00:23:06,960 --> 00:23:08,480
but only if you approach

659
00:23:08,480 --> 00:23:09,200
the work

660
00:23:09,200 --> 00:23:10,320
in the right spirit

661
00:23:10,320 --> 00:23:11,840
and with the right attitude.

662
